|      ∙ marks ({@<id>}) and the choice of an item with the arrow                |
|        keys. The user chooses an item only with its key;                       |
|      ∙ access checks (require). They need users;                               |
|      ∙ ask and a field token in an args value;                                 |
|      ∙ punctuation keys, for example ?;                                        |
|      ∙ a label of an item. The BBS does not print the text of an               |
|        item;                                                                   |
|      ∙ the table of contents of a Markdown file, active links to               |
|        other files, and syntax colours of source files;                        |
|      ∙ the display codes of other BBS programs: pipe codes, @ codes            |
|        and MCI codes. There is no converter.                                   |
|                                                                                |
|    Full rules: bbt-format, section 10, and file-view, section 12.              |
